(function(E){ const x = E["hr-m4"] = E["hr-m4"] || {units:{}}; x.units["hr-4-2"] = {"explain":{"id":"c-hr-4-2-e","course":"hr","unit":"hr-4-2","type":"explain","level":"B1","title":{"en":"Onboarding week","tr":"İşe uyum haftası","fa":"هفته‌ی اول کارمند تازه‌وارد"},"objective":{"en":"After this lesson, you can plan a new starter's first week and present it with clear times and deadlines.","tr":"Bu dersin sonunda yeni bir çalışanın ilk haftasını planlayıp net saatler ve son tarihlerle sunabileceksin.","fa":"بعد از این درس می‌توانی هفته‌ی اول یک کارمند تازه را برنامه‌ریزی کنی و آن را با ساعت‌ها و مهلت‌های روشن توضیح بدهی."},"hook":{"en":"Give a new starter a clear plan and one person to ask. Without them, people lose time and can feel alone. Leyla's plan had times, rooms and routes, and one little word that decides: finished by, or going on until?","tr":"Yeni çalışana net bir plan ve soracağı bir kişi ver. Bunlar olmadan zaman kaybeder ve kendini yalnız hissedebilir. Leyla'nın planında saatler, odalar ve rotalar vardı; bir de her şeyi belirleyen küçük bir kelime: o tarihe kadar bitecek mi (by), yoksa o tarihe kadar sürecek mi (until)?","fa":"به کارمند تازه‌وارد یک برنامه‌ی روشن و یک نفر برای پرسیدن بده. بدون این‌ها وقتش هدر می‌رود و ممکن است احساس تنهایی کند. برنامه‌ی لیلا ساعت و اتاق و مسیر داشت، و یک کلمه‌ی کوچک که همه چیز را تعیین می‌کند: تا آن موقع تمام شود (by)، یا تا آن موقع ادامه داشته باشد (until)؟"},"before":{"en":"Write a first-week plan for a new starter: one line a day, one deadline and the person to ask.","tr":"Yeni başlayan biri için ilk hafta planı yaz: her gün için bir satır, bir son tarih ve soru sorabileceği kişi.","fa":"برای یک کارمند تازه برنامه‌ی هفته‌ی اول بنویس: برای هر روز یک خط، یک مهلت و کسی که می‌تواند از او سؤال کند."},"rounds":[[1,4],[2,3]],"stats":[{"label":{"en":"Key points","tr":"Ana nokta","fa":"نکته‌ی اصلی"},"value":"4"},{"label":{"en":"Key phrases","tr":"Anahtar ifade","fa":"عبارت کلیدی"},"value":"4"},{"label":{"en":"Practice tasks","tr":"Alıştırma","fa":"تمرین"},"value":"4"}],"points":[{"eyebrow":{"en":"The skill","tr":"Beceri","fa":"مهارت"},"head":{"en":"One clear plan, one person to ask","tr":"Net bir plan, soracak bir kişi","fa":"یک برنامه‌ی روشن، یک نفر برای پرسیدن"},"body":{"en":"A new person can't guess how your company works. So say what happens each day, what has a deadline and who to ask. Put people in the plan, not only tasks.","tr":"Yeni biri şirketin nasıl işlediğini tahmin edemez. Bu yüzden her gün ne olacağını, neyin son tarihi olduğunu ve kime soracağını söyle. Plana yalnızca görevleri değil, insanları da koy.","fa":"آدم تازه‌وارد نمی‌تواند حدس بزند شرکت چطور کار می‌کند. پس بگو هر روز چه اتفاقی می‌افتد، چه چیزی مهلت دارد و از چه کسی بپرسد. در برنامه فقط کارها را نگذار، آدم‌ها را هم بگذار."}},{"eyebrow":{"en":"The language","tr":"Dil","fa":"زبان"},"head":{"en":"Planning a week: by, until, on, at","tr":"Bir haftayı planlamak: by, until, on, at","fa":"برنامه‌ریزی یک هفته: by، until، on، at"},"steps":[{"en":"A deadline, finished once: by.","tr":"Bir son tarih, bir kez biter: by.","fa":"برای مهلت و کاری که یک بار تمام می‌شود، by می‌آید.","ex":"Please complete the safety course by Friday."},{"en":"Goes on, then stops: until.","tr":"Devam eder, sonra durur: until.","fa":"برای کاری که ادامه دارد و بعد تمام می‌شود، until می‌آید.","ex":"You will shadow Hasan until Wednesday."},{"en":"Use on for a day and at for a clock time.","tr":"Gün için on, saat için at kullan.","fa":"برای روز on و برای ساعت at را به کار ببر.","ex":"on Monday at 8:30 / on Monday morning"},{"en":"Guide the reader: first, after that, then.","tr":"Okuru yönlendir: first, after that, then.","fa":"خواننده را راهنمایی کن: first، after that، ⁨then⁩.","ex":"First you'll get your badge. After that, ..."}],"table":{"headers":{"en":["Word","Use","Example"],"tr":["Sözcük","Kullanım","Örnek"],"fa":["کلمه","کاربرد","مثال"]},"rows":[["by","deadline: finished no later than","Complete the safety course by Friday."],["until","continues up to","You will shadow Hasan until Wednesday."],["on / at","day / clock time","On Monday at 8:30, meet Leyla on video."],["first, after that, then","order of steps","First you'll get your ID badge. After that..."]]},"tip":{"en":"Turkish -e kadar and Persian ta cover both by and until, so learners write 'finish it until Friday'. English splits them.","tr":"Türkçedeki '-e kadar' hem by hem until anlamına gelir; bu yüzden 'finish it until Friday' yazılır. İngilizce ikisini ayırır: by Friday (son tarih), until Friday (süre).","fa":"«تا» در فارسی هم معنی by را می‌دهد و هم until را؛ برای همین فارسی‌زبان‌ها می‌نویسند «finish it until Friday». انگلیسی این دو را جدا می‌کند: by Friday (مهلت)، until Friday (مدت)."},"wrong":"Please finish the forms until Wednesday.","right":"Please finish the forms by Wednesday."},{"eyebrow":{"en":"Key phrases","tr":"Anahtar ifadeler","fa":"عبارت‌های کلیدی"},"head":{"en":"Phrases for this task","tr":"Bu görev için ifadeler","fa":"عبارت‌های این کار"},"phrases":[{"phrase":"First you'll..., after that...","meaning":{"en":"Orders the steps.","tr":"Adımları sıralar.","fa":"مرحله‌ها را به ترتیب می‌چیند."}},{"phrase":"Please complete it by Friday.","meaning":{"en":"Gives a deadline.","tr":"Son tarih verir.","fa":"مهلت تعیین می‌کند."}},{"phrase":"If you have any questions, your buddy is...","meaning":{"en":"Names a person to ask.","tr":"Soru sorulacak kişiyi belirtir.","fa":"کسی را معرفی می‌کند که می‌شود از او سؤال کرد."}},{"phrase":"induction","meaning":{"en":"The formal introduction to a new job.","tr":"işe giriş eğitimi.","fa":"جلسه‌ی آموزش بدو ورود؛ معارفه‌ی رسمی"}}]},{"eyebrow":{"en":"At work","tr":"İş yerinde","fa":"در محیط کار"},"head":{"en":"A buddy, not only a manager","tr":"Sadece yönetici değil, bir de yol arkadaşı","fa":"یک همراه، نه فقط مدیر"},"body":{"en":"In many UK and US companies, a \"buddy\" (an informal helper who is not the new starter's manager) is a common part of onboarding. In more hierarchical workplaces, new staff may not ask simple questions to a manager at all, so a peer buddy is often the only safe person to ask where lunch is.","tr":"Birçok İngiliz ve Amerikan şirketinde \"buddy\" (yeni çalışanın yöneticisi olmayan gayriresmî bir yardımcı) işe uyumun yaygın bir parçasıdır. Daha hiyerarşik işyerlerinde yeni çalışanlar bir yöneticiye basit sorular hiç sormayabilir; bu yüzden öğle yemeğinin nerede yendiğini sormak için güvenli tek kişi çoğu zaman eşit düzeydeki bir buddy olur.","fa":"در بسیاری از شرکت‌های بریتانیا و آمریکا، داشتن یک buddy، یعنی همکار راهنمایی که مدیر فرد تازه‌وارد نیست، بخش رایجی از فرایند آشناسازی است. در محیط‌های کاری سلسله‌مراتبی‌تر، کارمند تازه ممکن است سؤال‌های ساده را اصلاً از مدیرش نپرسد؛ آن‌وقت همکار هم‌رده اغلب تنها کسی است که بی‌دغدغه می‌شود از او پرسید «ناهار کجاست؟»."}}],"example":{"eyebrow":{"en":"Worked example","tr":"Çözümlü örnek","fa":"مثال حل‌شده"},"head":{"en":"From weak to strong","tr":"Zayıftan güçlüye","fa":"از برنامه‌ی مبهم تا زمان و آدم و مهلت"},"text":"Facts: Monday at 9:00: meet the buddy. Forms are due by Wednesday.","item":"Come on Monday. Someone will show you everything.","why":{"en":"Weak: no time, no person. Strong: time, person, deadline.","tr":"Zayıf: zaman yok, kişi yok. Güçlü: zaman, kişi, son tarih.","fa":"نسخه‌ی اول نه زمان دارد، نه آدم. نسخه‌ی دوم زمان، آدم و مهلت دارد."},"answer":"On Monday at 9:00 you'll meet your buddy. Please finish the forms by Wednesday.","cut":["Someone will show you everything."],"cutHint":{"en":"Tap what tells the new starter nothing they can plan with.","tr":"Yeni başlayana plan yapabileceği hiçbir şey söylemeyen cümleye dokun.","fa":"روی جمله‌ای بزن که به کارمند تازه هیچ چیزی برای برنامه‌ریزی نمی‌گوید."}},"quick":{"prompt":"Why give a new starter a buddy as well as a manager?","options":["Some people feel safer asking a peer simple questions","The manager is too busy to meet them","A buddy checks their work"],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"Some people feel safer asking a peer: in more hierarchical workplaces, new staff may not ask a manager simple questions at all.","tr":"Bazı insanlar basit soruları bir çalışma arkadaşına sormayı daha güvenli bulur: Daha hiyerarşik iş yerlerinde yeni çalışanlar yöneticiye basit sorular hiç sormayabilir.","fa":"بعضی‌ها پرسیدن سؤال‌های ساده از یک همکار را امن‌تر می‌دانند: در محیط‌های سلسله‌مراتبی‌تر، کارمند تازه ممکن است اصلاً سؤال ساده را از مدیر نپرسد."},"point":4},"remember":{"en":"Does the action happen once and finish? by. Does it continue and then stop? until. Result of this lesson: you can plan and present a first week. You also have the written plan.","tr":"Eylem bir kez olup bitiyor mu? by. Devam edip sonra duruyor mu? until. Bu dersin sonucu: bir ilk haftayı planlayıp sunabilirsin ve elinde yazılı plan olur.","fa":"کار یک بار انجام می‌شود و تمام می‌شود؟ by. ادامه دارد و بعد می‌ایستد؟ ⁨until⁩. حالا می‌توانی هفته‌ی اول را برنامه‌ریزی کنی و توضیح بدهی. برنامه‌ی نوشته‌شده هم آماده است."},"b2Point":{"eyebrow":{"en":"B2 track","tr":"B2 yolu","fa":"مسیر B2"},"head":{"en":"Future perfect: By Friday you'll have met...","tr":"Gelecekte tamamlanmış zaman (future perfect): By Friday you'll have met...","fa":"آینده‌ی کامل: By Friday you’ll have met..."},"steps":[{"en":"Done before a future point: will have + past participle.","tr":"Gelecekteki bir andan önce bitmiş: will have + past participle.","fa":"وقتی می‌گویی کاری تا زمان مشخصی در آینده تمام شده است، will have و اسم مفعول می‌آوری.","ex":"By Friday you'll have met the whole team."},{"en":"It almost always comes with by.","tr":"Neredeyse her zaman by ile gelir.","fa":"تقریباً همیشه با by می‌آید.","ex":"by the end of your first month"},{"en":"Use it to reassure: show the progress ahead.","tr":"Güven vermek için kullan: önündeki ilerlemeyi göster.","fa":"برای دلگرمی دادن هم به کار می‌رود: پیشرفتی را که در راه است نشان می‌دهد.","ex":"By Friday you'll have driven your first route."}],"table":{"headers":{"en":["Deadline","Future perfect"],"tr":["Son tarih","Future perfect"],"fa":["مهلت","آینده‌ی کامل"]},"rows":[["By Friday,","you'll have met the whole team."],["By the end of the week,","you'll have driven your first route."],["By the end of your first month,","you'll have finished all the training."]]},"body":{"en":"B2 track: end your welcome message with two future perfect sentences that show what the new starter will have done by Friday.","tr":"B2 yolu: hoş geldin mesajını, yeni çalışanın cumaya kadar neleri yapmış olacağını gösteren iki future perfect cümlesiyle bitir.","fa":"مسیر B2: پیام خوشامدت را با دو جمله در زمان آینده‌ی کامل تمام کن که نشان دهد تازه‌وارد تا جمعه چه کارهایی را انجام داده است."}}},"grammar":{"id":"c-hr-4-2-g","level":"B1","course":"hr","unit":"hr-4-2","title":"Planning a week: by, until, on, at","titleTr":"Bir haftayı planlamak: by, until, on, at","exp":{"en":"A first-week plan is a list of times and deadlines, so small time words matter. By = no later than (a deadline for something to be finished): \"Please complete the safety course by Friday.\" Until = all the time up to that point (something continues): \"You will shadow Hasan until Wednesday.\" Turkish \"-e kadar\" and Farsi «تا» cover both, so learners often say \"until Friday\" for a deadline. Test: if the action finishes once, use by; if it goes on and then stops, use until. Also: on + day (\"on Monday\"), at + clock time (\"at 8:30\"), and no preposition before morning when there is a day: \"on Monday morning\", not \"on Monday at the morning\". Sequence words make the plan easy to follow: first, after that, then, by the end of the week.","tr":"İlk hafta planı saatler ve son tarihlerden oluşan bir listedir, bu yüzden küçük zaman sözcükleri önemlidir. By = en geç (bitmesi gereken bir şey için son tarih): \"Please complete the safety course by Friday.\" Until = o ana kadar tüm süre boyunca (bir şey devam eder): \"You will shadow Hasan until Wednesday.\" Türkçedeki \"-e kadar\" ikisini de karşıladığı için öğrenciler son tarih için de \"until Friday\" der. Test: eylem bir kez bitiyorsa by; devam edip sonra duruyorsa until. Ayrıca: gün için on (\"on Monday\"), saat için at (\"at 8:30\") ve gün varsa morning'den önce edat yok: \"on Monday morning\", \"on Monday at the morning\" değil. Sıra sözcükleri planı takip etmeyi kolaylaştırır: first, after that, then, by the end of the week.","fa":"برنامه‌ی هفته‌ی اول پر از ساعت و مهلت است؛ پس کلمه‌های کوچکِ زمانی اهمیت زیادی دارند. by یعنی «حداکثر تا» و برای مهلتِ کاری است که باید تا آن زمان تمام شود: «⁨Please complete the safety course by Friday.⁩» until یعنی «تمام مدت تا» و برای کاری است که تا آن زمان ادامه دارد: «⁨You will shadow Hasan until Wednesday.⁩» در فارسی «تا» هر دو معنا را می‌رساند، برای همین فارسی‌زبان‌ها برای مهلت هم می‌گویند «until Friday». آزمون ساده: اگر کار یک بار انجام و تمام می‌شود، by؛ اگر ادامه دارد و در آن زمان قطع می‌شود، until. چند نکته‌ی دیگر: on + روز («on Monday»)، at + ساعت («at 8:30») و وقتی روز را گفته‌ای، قبل از morning حرف اضافه نمی‌آید: «on Monday morning»، نه «on Monday at the morning». کلمه‌های ترتیب هم برنامه را قابل دنبال کردن می‌کنند: first، after that، then و by the end of the week."},"formsTable":{"headers":{"en":["Word","Use","Example"],"tr":["Sözcük","Kullanım","Örnek"],"fa":["کلمه","کاربرد","مثال"]},"rows":[["by","deadline: finished no later than","Complete the safety course by Friday."],["until","continues up to","You will shadow Hasan until Wednesday."],["on / at","day / clock time","On Monday at 8:30, meet Leyla on video."],["first, after that, then","order of steps","First you'll get your ID badge. After that..."]]},"wrong":"Please finish the safety course until Friday.","right":"Please finish the safety course by Friday.","blank":{"sentence":"Please complete the safety training ___ Friday.","word":"by","distractors":["until","since"]},"wrong2":"On Monday at the morning, you will meet the team.","right2":"On Monday morning, you will meet the team.","blank2":{"sentence":"You will shadow Hasan ___ Wednesday.","word":"until","distractors":["by","since"]},"expParts":{"tryFrom":"blank","hook":{"en":"Leyla's plan had times, rooms and routes, and one little word that decides: finished by, or going on until?","tr":"Leyla'nın planında saatler, odalar ve rotalar vardı; bir de her şeyi belirleyen küçük bir kelime: o tarihe kadar bitecek mi (by), yoksa o tarihe kadar sürecek mi (until)?","fa":"برنامه‌ی لیلا ساعت و اتاق و مسیر داشت، و یک کلمه‌ی کوچک که همه چیز را تعیین می‌کند: تا آن موقع تمام شود (by)، یا تا آن موقع ادامه داشته باشد (until)؟"},"tryWhy":{"en":"by: the training is finished once, no later than Friday. until would mean it goes on all week.","tr":"by: eğitim bir kez tamamlanır, en geç cuma. until olsaydı bütün hafta sürerdi.","fa":"جواب by است: آموزش یک بار تمام می‌شود، حداکثر تا جمعه. until یعنی تمام هفته ادامه دارد."},"rule":[{"en":"A deadline, finished once: by.","tr":"Bir son tarih, bir kez biter: by.","fa":"برای مهلت و کاری که یک بار تمام می‌شود، by می‌آید.","ex":"Please complete the safety course by Friday."},{"en":"Goes on, then stops: until.","tr":"Devam eder, sonra durur: until.","fa":"برای کاری که ادامه دارد و بعد تمام می‌شود، until می‌آید.","ex":"You will shadow Hasan until Wednesday."},{"en":"on + day; at + clock time; on Monday morning.","tr":"on + gün; at + saat; on Monday morning.","fa":"برای روز on می‌آید و برای ساعت at؛ مثلاً on Monday morning.","ex":"on Monday at 8:30 / on Monday morning"},{"en":"Guide the reader: first, after that, then.","tr":"Okuru yönlendir: first, after that, then.","fa":"خواننده را راهنمایی کن: first، after that، ⁨then⁩.","ex":"First you'll get your badge. After that, ..."}],"test":{"en":"Does the action happen once and finish? by. Does it continue and then stop? until.","tr":"Eylem bir kez olup bitiyor mu? by. Devam edip sonra duruyor mu? until.","fa":"کار یک بار انجام می‌شود و تمام می‌شود؟ by. ادامه دارد و بعد می‌ایستد؟ ⁨until⁩."},"contrast":{"en":"Turkish -e kadar and Persian ta cover both by and until, so learners write 'finish it until Friday'. English splits them.","tr":"Türkçedeki '-e kadar' hem by hem until anlamına gelir; bu yüzden 'finish it until Friday' yazılır. İngilizce ikisini ayırır: by Friday (son tarih), until Friday (süre).","fa":"«تا» در فارسی هم معنی by را می‌دهد و هم until را؛ برای همین فارسی‌زبان‌ها می‌نویسند «finish it until Friday». انگلیسی این دو را جدا می‌کند: by Friday (مهلت)، until Friday (مدت)."}},"errorWatch":[{"find":["complete it until","finish it until","complete the course until","finish the course until","finish the safety course until","complete the training until","submit it until","send it until","send me until"],"fix":{"en":"For a deadline use by: 'Please complete it by Friday.'","tr":"Son tarih için by kullan: 'Please complete it by Friday.'","fa":"برای مهلت by بنویس: «⁨Please complete it by Friday.⁩»"}},{"find":["at the morning","at the afternoon","in monday","at monday","on monday at the"],"fix":{"en":"on + day, at + time, in the morning: 'on Monday morning', 'on Monday at 8:30'.","tr":"on + gün, at + saat, in the morning: 'on Monday morning', 'on Monday at 8:30'.","fa":"برای روز on، برای ساعت at و in the morning: «on Monday morning» و «on Monday at 8:30»."}}]},"b2":{"id":"c-hr-4-2-b2","level":"B2","track":"B2","course":"hr","unit":"hr-4-2","title":"Future perfect: By Friday you'll have met...","titleTr":"Future perfect: By Friday you'll have met...","exp":{"en":"The future perfect (will have + past participle) looks back from a point in the future: \"By Friday you'll have met the whole team.\" It is perfect for onboarding messages because it shows progress and reassures the new person: by a certain day, these things will be done. It almost always comes with by (\"by Friday\", \"by the end of your first month\"). Keep all three parts: will + have + past participle. Not \"will have meet\", not \"will finished\".","tr":"Future perfect (will have + past participle) gelecekteki bir noktadan geriye bakar: \"By Friday you'll have met the whole team.\" İşe uyum mesajları için idealdir, çünkü ilerlemeyi gösterir ve yeni kişiye güven verir: belli bir güne kadar bunlar bitmiş olacak. Türkçedeki \"-miş olacaksın\" yapısına benzer. Neredeyse her zaman by ile gelir (\"by Friday\", \"by the end of your first month\"). Üç parçayı da koru: will + have + past participle. \"will have meet\" değil, \"will finished\" değil.","fa":"آینده‌ی کامل (future perfect) یعنی will have + اسم مفعول، از یک نقطه در آینده به عقب نگاه می‌کند: «⁨By Friday you'll have met the whole team.⁩» یعنی «تا جمعه با همه‌ی اعضای تیم آشنا شده‌اید». این ساختار برای پیام خوشامد عالی است، چون پیشرفت را نشان می‌دهد و به تازه‌وارد اطمینان می‌دهد که تا روزی مشخص این کارها انجام شده است. تقریباً همیشه با by می‌آید («by Friday»، «by the end of your first month»). هر سه جزء را حفظ کن: will + have + اسم مفعول. نه «will have meet» و نه «will finished»."},"formsTable":{"headers":{"en":["Deadline","Future perfect"],"tr":["Son tarih","Future perfect"],"fa":["مهلت","آینده‌ی کامل"]},"rows":[["By Friday,","you'll have met the whole team."],["By the end of the week,","you'll have driven your first route."],["By the end of your first month,","you'll have finished all the training."]]},"wrong":"By Friday you will have meet the whole team.","right":"By Friday you will have met the whole team.","blank":{"sentence":"By Friday you ___ the whole team.","word":"will have met","distractors":["will have meet","have met"]},"wrong2":"By Friday, you will finished the safety course.","right2":"By Friday, you will have finished the safety course.","blank2":{"sentence":"By the end of the week, Deniz will have ___ his first route.","word":"driven","distractors":["drove","drive"]},"useIn":{"en":"B2 track: end your welcome message with two future perfect sentences that show what the new starter will have done by Friday.","tr":"B2 yolu: hoş geldin mesajını, yeni çalışanın cumaya kadar neleri yapmış olacağını gösteren iki future perfect cümlesiyle bitir.","fa":"مسیر B2: پیام خوشامدت را با دو جمله در زمان آینده‌ی کامل تمام کن که نشان دهد تازه‌وارد تا جمعه چه کارهایی را انجام داده است."},"exitItem":{"from":"hr-4-2","kind":"blank","prompt":"By the end of the week, you ___ all five routes.","options":["will have driven","will have drive","have driven"],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"will have driven: 'by the end of the week' means finished before then: will have + past participle. 'Will have drive' drops the participle, and 'have driven' is about now.","tr":"will have driven: 'by the end of the week' o zamana kadar bitmiş demektir: will have + üçüncü hâl. 'Will have drive' üçüncü hâli düşürür; 'have driven' şimdiyle ilgilidir.","fa":"will have driven درست است، چون by the end of the week یعنی تا آن موقع تمام شده: will have و اسم مفعول. will have drive اسم مفعول ندارد و have driven درباره‌ی الان است."}},"expParts":{"hook":{"en":"'By Friday you'll have met the whole team.' One sentence that tells a nervous new starter: you will be fine.","tr":"'By Friday you'll have met the whole team.' Gergin bir yeni çalışana 'merak etme, olacak' diyen tek bir cümle.","fa":"«⁨By Friday you'll have met the whole team.⁩» یک جمله که به یک تازه‌وارد نگران می‌گوید: همه چیز روبه‌راه می‌شود."},"tryWhy":{"en":"driven: will have needs the past participle. drive is the base form and drove is the past simple.","tr":"driven: will have'den sonra past participle gelir. drive yalın hâl, drove ise past simple.","fa":"جواب driven است: بعد از will have اسم مفعول می‌آید. drive شکل ساده است و drove گذشته‌ی ساده."},"rule":[{"en":"Done before a future point: will have + past participle.","tr":"Gelecekteki bir andan önce bitmiş: will have + past participle.","fa":"وقتی می‌گویی کاری تا زمان مشخصی در آینده تمام شده است، will have و اسم مفعول می‌آوری.","ex":"By Friday you'll have met the whole team."},{"en":"It almost always comes with by.","tr":"Neredeyse her zaman by ile gelir.","fa":"تقریباً همیشه با by می‌آید.","ex":"by the end of your first month"},{"en":"Use it to reassure: show the progress ahead.","tr":"Güven vermek için kullan: önündeki ilerlemeyi göster.","fa":"برای دلگرمی دادن هم به کار می‌رود: پیشرفتی را که در راه است نشان می‌دهد.","ex":"By Friday you'll have driven your first route."}],"test":{"en":"Count three parts: will, have, past participle (met, driven, finished). Missing one? Add it.","tr":"Üç parçayı say: will, have, past participle (met, driven, finished). Biri eksik mi? Ekle.","fa":"سه بخش را بشمار: will، have و اسم مفعول (met، driven، finished). یکی کم است؟ اضافه‌اش کن."},"contrast":{"en":"Turkish tanışmış olacaksın and Persian ashna shode-i match this form well. The trap is only the past participle: met, not meet.","tr":"Türkçedeki 'tanışmış olacaksın' bu yapıya çok yakındır. Tek tuzak past participle'dır: meet değil met.","fa":"در فارسی می‌گوییم «تا جمعه با همه آشنا شده‌ای» که خیلی به این ساختار نزدیک است. تنها تله اسم مفعول است: met، نه ⁨meet⁩."}},"errorWatch":[{"find":["will have meet","will have drive","will have finish","will have drove","you'll have meet","will finished","will met"],"fix":{"en":"Use will have + past participle: 'By Friday you'll have met the whole team.'","tr":"will have + past participle kullan: 'By Friday you'll have met the whole team.'","fa":"از will have و اسم مفعول استفاده کن: «By Friday you'll have met the whole team.»"}}]},"vocab":{"id":"c-hr-4-2-v","level":"B1","category":"vocab","course":"hr","unit":"hr-4-2","goals":["career"],"title":{"en":"Onboarding","tr":"İşe Uyum","fa":"ورود و آشناسازی کارمند جدید"},"cards":[{"word":"onboarding","sentence":"Good onboarding helps new staff stay longer.","meaning":{"en":"Helping a new employee start and fit in.","tr":"işe alıştırma, oryantasyon.","fa":"فرایند ورود و آشناسازی کارمند جدید (onboarding)"}},{"word":"induction","sentence":"Monday is induction day: rules, tour and ID badge.","meaning":{"en":"The formal introduction to a new job.","tr":"işe giriş eğitimi.","fa":"جلسه‌ی آموزش بدو ورود؛ معارفه‌ی رسمی"}},{"word":"shadow","sentence":"You will shadow Hasan on his route.","meaning":{"en":"To follow someone to learn how they work.","tr":"birinin yanında çalışarak öğrenmek.","fa":"کنار کسی کار کردن تا روش کارش را یاد بگیری"}},{"word":"buddy","sentence":"Hasan is your buddy for the first month.","meaning":{"en":"A colleague who helps a new person informally.","tr":"rehber çalışan (buddy); yeni gelene destek olan iş arkadaşı.","fa":"همکار راهنما (کسی که غیررسمی به تازه‌وارد کمک می‌کند)"}},{"word":"welcome pack","sentence":"Your welcome pack has a map and key phone numbers.","meaning":{"en":"Information given to a new starter.","tr":"hoş geldin paketi.","fa":"بسته‌ی خوشامدگویی (اطلاعاتی که به تازه‌وارد داده می‌شود)"}},{"word":"ID badge","sentence":"Wear your ID badge in the warehouse.","meaning":{"en":"A card with your name and photo.","tr":"kimlik kartı.","fa":"کارت شناسایی پرسنلی"}},{"word":"safety training","sentence":"Safety training takes four hours.","meaning":{"en":"A course about working safely.","tr":"iş güvenliği eğitimi.","fa":"آموزش ایمنی"}},{"word":"settle in","sentence":"It takes a few weeks to settle in.","meaning":{"en":"To start to feel comfortable in a new place.","tr":"alışmak, yerleşmek.","fa":"جا افتادن؛ کم‌کم در محیط تازه راحت شدن"}},{"word":"check-in","sentence":"We'll have a short check-in on Friday.","meaning":{"en":"A short meeting to see how things are going.","tr":"kısa durum görüşmesi.","fa":"جلسه‌ی کوتاه پیگیری («کارها چطور پیش می‌رود؟»)"}},{"word":"belong","sentence":"People stay where they feel they belong.","meaning":{"en":"To feel part of a group.","tr":"ait olmak.","fa":"احساس تعلق کردن؛ خود را جزئی از گروه دانستن"}}]},"story":{"id":"c-hr-4-2-s","level":"B1","genre":"Workplace","course":"hr","unit":"hr-4-2","title":{"en":"Thursday Lunch","tr":"Perşembe Öğle Yemeği","fa":"ناهار پنجشنبه"},"text":"Leyla's plan for Deniz's first week looked perfect. Monday: induction and ID badge. Tuesday: safety training, to be completed by the end of the day. Wednesday and Thursday: shadow Hasan on Route 7. Friday: first route alone, then a check-in with Leyla at 4 p.m.\n\nOn Wednesday she called him. \"How's it going?\"\n\n\"Good, good,\" said Deniz. \"Everything is clear.\"\n\nAn hour later a message arrived from Hasan. \"Your new guy is good on the road. But he eats lunch alone in his truck. Every day.\"\n\nLeyla looked at her plan again. It had times, rooms, rules and routes. It did not have one person in it, except as a task. Nobody had told Deniz where the drivers ate, or that they ate together at all.\n\nShe called Hasan back. \"Could you be his buddy until the end of the month? And is there a team lunch this week?\"\n\n\"Thursday,\" said Hasan. \"Grilled chicken. Very loud.\"\n\nOn Thursday Hasan didn't ask. He just took Deniz's arm at twelve and walked him to the long table. Someone asked about the Izmit truck story, which Hasan had already told everyone. Deniz told it again, with the hospital part. The table went quiet, and then somebody clapped him on the back.\n\nAt Friday's check-in, Leyla asked her last question. \"What would make you feel you belong here?\"\n\nDeniz thought for a moment. \"Thursday,\" he said. \"More Thursdays.\"\n\nThat evening Leyla added a new line to every first-week plan she would ever write: Day 1, 12:00, lunch with your buddy.","vocab":[{"word":"route","en":"The way a driver goes every day.","tr":"güzergâh","fa":"مسیر هر روزه‌ی راننده"},{"word":"except","en":"But not; apart from.","tr":"hariç","fa":"به‌جز"},{"word":"grilled","en":"Cooked over strong heat.","tr":"ızgara","fa":"کبابی؛ گریل‌شده"},{"word":"clap someone on the back","en":"To hit someone's back lightly, in a friendly way.","tr":"birinin sırtını dostça sıvazlamak","fa":"دوستانه به پشت کسی زدن"},{"word":"loud","en":"Making a lot of noise.","tr":"gürültülü","fa":"پرسروصدا"}],"quiz":[{"prompt":"What was missing from Leyla's first plan?","options":["Safety training","People and belonging","A deadline"],"correct":1},{"prompt":"Choose the correct sentence.","options":["Hasan will be his buddy by the end of the month.","Hasan will be his buddy until the end of the month.","Hasan will be his buddy since the end of the month."],"correct":1},{"prompt":"What new line did Leyla add to every plan?","options":["Day 1, 12:00, lunch with your buddy","Day 1, safety test","Day 5, first route alone"],"correct":0},{"prompt":"Why did Deniz say \"Everything is clear\" on Wednesday?","options":["He did not want to complain in his first week","He had no problems at all","Hasan told him to say it"],"correct":0}],"notice":{"en":"Leyla's first-week plan looks perfect. Read it, then read Hasan's message. What is missing from the plan?","tr":"Leyla'nın ilk hafta planı kusursuz görünüyor. Önce planı, sonra Hasan'ın mesajını oku. Planda ne eksik?","fa":"برنامه‌ی هفته‌ی اول لیلا بی‌نقص به نظر می‌رسد. برنامه را بخوان و بعد پیام حسن را. چه چیزی در برنامه کم است؟"},"bridge":{"en":"'Complete it by the end of the day.' 'Be his buddy until the end of the month.' Next: see the difference.","tr":"'Complete it by the end of the day.' 'Be his buddy until the end of the month.' Sırada: farkı gör.","fa":"«⁨Complete it by the end of the day.⁩» و «⁨Be his buddy until the end of the month.⁩» قدم بعد: تفاوتشان را ببین."}},"speaking":{"id":"hr-4-2","course":"hr","unit":"hr-4-2","topic":{"en":"Presenting a First-Week Plan","tr":"İlk Hafta Planını Sunmak","fa":"ارائه‌ی برنامه‌ی هفته‌ی اول"},"warmup":{"en":"What happened on your first day at your current or last job? What do you wish someone had done?","tr":"Şu anki ya da son işindeki ilk gününde ne oldu? Keşke biri ne yapsaydı diyorsun?","fa":"روز اول کار فعلی یا آخرین کارت چطور گذشت؟ دلت می‌خواست کسی چه کاری برایت بکند؟"},"questions":[{"en":"Walk Deniz through Monday to Friday. Use first, after that, then.","tr":"Deniz'e pazartesiden cumaya planı anlat. First, after that, then kullan.","fa":"برنامه‌ی دوشنبه تا جمعه را قدم‌به‌قدم برای دنیز توضیح بده. از first، after that و then استفاده کن."},{"en":"Give one deadline with by and one ongoing arrangement with until.","tr":"By ile bir son tarih ve until ile süren bir düzenleme söyle.","fa":"یک مهلت با by و یک برنامه‌ی ادامه‌دار با until بگو."},{"en":"Introduce his buddy and say when they will have lunch together.","tr":"Rehber çalışanını (buddy) tanıt ve ne zaman birlikte öğle yemeği yiyeceklerini söyle.","fa":"همکار راهنمای دنیز را معرفی کن و بگو کی با هم ناهار می‌خورند."}],"followups":[{"en":"Present the plan in 90 seconds, then 60, then 45.","tr":"Planı 90, sonra 60, sonra 45 saniyede sun.","fa":"برنامه را یک بار در ۹۰ ثانیه، بعد در ۶۰ و بعد در ۴۵ ثانیه ارائه بده."},{"en":"Now plan the first day of a new person at your workplace, with times.","tr":"Şimdi iş yerine yeni gelen birinin ilk gününü saatleriyle planla.","fa":"حالا روز اول یک همکار جدید را در محل کارت ساعت‌به‌ساعت برنامه‌ریزی کن."}],"expressions":[{"phrase":"First you'll..., after that...","meaning":{"en":"Orders the steps.","tr":"Adımları sıralar.","fa":"مرحله‌ها را به ترتیب می‌چیند."}},{"phrase":"Please complete it by Friday.","meaning":{"en":"Gives a deadline.","tr":"Son tarih verir.","fa":"مهلت تعیین می‌کند."}},{"phrase":"If you have any questions, your buddy is...","meaning":{"en":"Names a person to ask.","tr":"Soru sorulacak kişiyi belirtir.","fa":"کسی را معرفی می‌کند که می‌شود از او سؤال کرد."}}],"culture":{"en":"In many UK and US companies, a \"buddy\" (an informal helper who is not the new starter's manager) is a common part of onboarding. In more hierarchical workplaces, new staff may not ask simple questions to a manager at all, so a peer buddy is often the only safe person to ask where lunch is.","tr":"Birçok İngiliz ve Amerikan şirketinde \"buddy\" (yeni çalışanın yöneticisi olmayan gayriresmî bir yardımcı) işe uyumun yaygın bir parçasıdır. Daha hiyerarşik işyerlerinde yeni çalışanlar bir yöneticiye basit sorular hiç sormayabilir; bu yüzden öğle yemeğinin nerede yendiğini sormak için güvenli tek kişi çoğu zaman eşit düzeydeki bir buddy olur.","fa":"در بسیاری از شرکت‌های بریتانیا و آمریکا، داشتن یک buddy، یعنی همکار راهنمایی که مدیر فرد تازه‌وارد نیست، بخش رایجی از فرایند آشناسازی است. در محیط‌های کاری سلسله‌مراتبی‌تر، کارمند تازه ممکن است سؤال‌های ساده را اصلاً از مدیرش نپرسد؛ آن‌وقت همکار هم‌رده اغلب تنها کسی است که بی‌دغدغه می‌شود از او پرسید «ناهار کجاست؟»."},"model":"Welcome, Deniz. Here is your first week. First, on Monday at 8:30, you'll have your induction and your ID badge. After that, at twelve, you'll have lunch with Hasan, your buddy. On Tuesday you'll do the safety training. Please complete it by 5 p.m. Then you'll shadow Hasan until Thursday. On Friday you'll drive your first route alone, and we'll have a check-in at four.","selfCheck":[{"en":"I went through the days in order with first, after that, then.","tr":"Günleri first, after that, then ile sırayla anlattım.","fa":"روزها را به ترتیب با first، after that و then گفتم."},{"en":"I used by for a deadline and until for something ongoing.","tr":"Son tarih için by, süren bir şey için until kullandım.","fa":"برای مهلت by و برای کار ادامه‌دار until به کار بردم."},{"en":"I introduced the buddy and the lunch.","tr":"Buddy'yi ve öğle yemeğini tanıttım.","fa":"همکار راهنما و ناهار را معرفی کردم."},{"en":"I used on with days and at with times.","tr":"Günlerle on, saatlerle at kullandım.","fa":"با روزها on و با ساعت‌ها at به کار بردم."}]},"writing":{"id":"c-hr-4-2-w","title":{"en":"A first-week plan for a new driver","tr":"Yeni sürücü için ilk hafta planı","fa":"برنامه‌ی هفته‌ی اول برای راننده‌ی تازه‌وارد"},"course":"hr","unit":"hr-4-2","type":"writing","difficulty":"medium","prompt":{"en":"Write a first-week plan and welcome message for a new starter (70-100 words): a warm opening, one line per day Monday to Friday, one deadline with by, the buddy, and a Friday check-in.","tr":"Yeni başlayan biri için ilk hafta planı ve hoş geldin mesajı yaz (70-100 kelime): sıcak bir giriş, pazartesiden cumaya her gün için bir satır, by ile bir son tarih, rehber çalışan (buddy) ve cuma günü kısa görüşme.","fa":"برای یک کارمند تازه‌وارد، برنامه‌ی هفته‌ی اول و پیام خوشامد بنویس (۷۰ تا ۱۰۰ کلمه): یک شروع گرم، برای هر روز از دوشنبه تا جمعه یک خط، یک مهلت با by، معرفی همکار راهنما و یک جلسه‌ی کوتاه پیگیری در روز جمعه."},"model":"Welcome to Atlas, Deniz! We are very happy to have you in the Dubai team. Here is your first week. Monday: induction at 8:30, then your ID badge and a tour. Tuesday: safety training; please complete it by 5 p.m. Wednesday and Thursday: you will shadow Hasan on Route 7. Hasan is your buddy until the end of April, and he will take you to lunch on Monday. Friday: your first route alone, then a short check-in with me at 4 p.m. See you on Monday! Leyla","frame":"Welcome to ___, ___! We are ___. Here is your first week. Monday: ___ at ___, then ___. Tuesday: ___; please complete it by ___. Wednesday and Thursday: you will ___. ___ is your buddy until ___. Friday: ___, then a check-in with ___ at ___. See you ___!","words":[{"word":"by"},{"word":"until"},{"word":"buddy"}],"minWords":70,"minSentences":7,"rubric":["Task done: welcome, 5 days, a by-deadline, buddy, check-in","Organised: day by day, easy to scan","Language: by vs until; on/at; will for the plan","Tone: warm; the new starter feels expected, not processed"],"rubricI18n":{"tr":["Görev: karşılama, 5 gün, by ile verilmiş bir son tarih, buddy, ara görüşme","Düzen: gün gün, kolay göz atılır","Dil: by ve until farkı; on/at; plan için will","Üslup: sıcak; yeni çalışan beklendiğini hisseder, bir dosya gibi işlenmez"],"fa":["کامل بودن کار: خوشامد، پنج روز، یک مهلت با by، همکار راهنما، جلسه‌ی پیگیری","روزبه‌روز، طوری که با یک نگاه خوانده شود","زبان: تفاوت by و until؛ on/at؛ will برای برنامه","لحن: گرم؛ تازه‌وارد حس کند منتظرش بوده‌اند، نه اینکه فقط کارهای اداری‌اش را انجام داده‌اند"]},"portfolio":"hr-final-6","parts":[{"t":{"en":"A warm opening","tr":"Sıcak bir açılış","fa":"شروعی گرم"},"find":["welcome","happy to have you"],"sample":"Welcome to Atlas! We are happy to have you"},{"t":{"en":"One line for each day","tr":"Her gün için bir satır","fa":"برای هر روز یک خط"},"find":["monday","tuesday","wednesday","friday"],"sample":"Mon induction; Tue safety; Wed-Thu shadow Hasan; Fri first route"},{"t":{"en":"One deadline with by","tr":"by ile bir son tarih","fa":"یک مهلت با ⁨by⁩"},"find":["by"],"sample":"safety training by 5 p.m. on Tuesday"},{"t":{"en":"The buddy","tr":"Destekçi iş arkadaşı","fa":"همکار راهنما"},"find":["buddy"],"sample":"Hasan, until the end of April"},{"t":{"en":"A Friday check-in","tr":"Cuma günü kısa bir görüşme","fa":"یک گفتگوی کوتاه در جمعه"},"find":["check-in","check in"],"sample":"Friday at 4 p.m. with me"}]},"perspective":{"id":"c-hr-4-2-p","title":{"en":"Deniz eating lunch alone","tr":"Öğle yemeğini tek başına yiyen Deniz","fa":"دنیز که تنها ناهار می‌خورد"},"course":"hr","unit":"hr-4-2","type":"perspective","minSentences":2,"prompt":{"en":"You are Deniz on day 3, eating lunch alone in the truck. Write 2-3 sentences in first person: what would make you feel that you belong here?","tr":"Üçüncü günündeki Deniz'sin, öğle yemeğini kamyonda yalnız yiyorsun. Birinci tekil şahısla 2-3 cümle yaz: buraya ait olduğunu hissetmeni ne sağlardı?","fa":"تو دنیز هستی. روز سوم است و ناهارت را تنهایی توی کامیون می‌خوری. از زبان خودت دو یا سه جمله بنویس: چه چیزی باعث می‌شود حس کنی به این جمع تعلق داری؟"}},"exit":{"id":"c-hr-4-2-x","course":"hr","unit":"hr-4-2","type":"exit","items":[{"from":"hr-4-2","kind":"blank","prompt":"Your uniform will be ready ___ Tuesday.","options":["by","since","until"],"correct":0,"point":2,"why":{"en":"by: 'by Tuesday' means no later than Tuesday. 'Since' looks back from now, and 'until' is the whole time up to Tuesday.","tr":"by: 'by Tuesday' en geç salı demektir. 'Since' şimdiden geriye bakar; 'until' salıya kadar bütün süredir.","fa":"by درست است، چون by Tuesday یعنی حداکثر تا سه‌شنبه. since از الان به عقب نگاه می‌کند و until تمام مدت تا سه‌شنبه است."},"hint2":{"en":"Being ready happens once, at the latest on that day. Which word gives a deadline?","tr":"Bu, bir kez ve en geç o gün olacak bir şey. Hangi kelime son tarih bildirir?","fa":"آماده شدن یک بار و حداکثر تا آن روز اتفاق می‌افتد. کدام کلمه مهلت را نشان می‌دهد؟"}},{"from":"hr-4-2","kind":"blank","prompt":"The induction starts ___ 8:30.","options":["on","at","by"],"correct":1,"point":2,"why":{"en":"at: 'at' goes with clock times. 'On' is for days and dates, and 'by' means no later than.","tr":"at: 'at' saatlerle kullanılır. 'On' günler ve tarihler içindir; 'by' en geç demektir.","fa":"at درست است، چون at با ساعت می‌آید. on برای روز و تاریخ است و by یعنی حداکثر تا."},"hint2":{"en":"8:30 is a clock time. Which word goes before a clock time?","tr":"8:30 bir saat. Saatlerden önce hangi kelime gelir?","fa":"۸:۳۰ یک ساعت است. قبل از ساعت کدام کلمه می‌آید؟"}},{"from":"hr-4-2","kind":"mcq","prompt":"Which line is correct?","options":["On Monday morning, you will meet the team.","On Monday at the morning, you will meet the team.","In Monday morning, you will meet the team."],"correct":0,"point":2,"why":{"en":"'On Monday morning': a day plus a part of the day takes on, with no 'the'. 'At the morning' and 'in Monday morning' are wrong.","tr":"'On Monday morning': gün + günün bir kısmı on alır ve 'the' gelmez. 'At the morning' ve 'in Monday morning' yanlıştır.","fa":"«On Monday morning» درست است، چون روز همراه بخشی از روز با on می‌آید و the نمی‌خواهد. at the morning و in Monday morning غلط‌اند."}},{"from":"hr-4-1","kind":"blank","prompt":"You are not allowed ___ in the trucks.","options":["smoke","to smoke","smoking"],"correct":1,"point":2,"why":{"en":"to smoke: 'be allowed' takes to + verb. 'Smoke' drops to, and 'smoking' doesn't follow allowed this way.","tr":"to smoke: 'be allowed' to + fiil alır. 'Smoke' to'yu düşürür; 'smoking' allowed'dan sonra bu şekilde gelmez.","fa":"to smoke درست است، چون be allowed با to و فعل می‌آید. smoke بدون to است و smoking این‌طور بعد از allowed نمی‌آید."}},{"from":"hr-3-3","kind":"blank","prompt":"She ___ she had led a team of four.","options":["said","told","said me"],"correct":0,"point":2,"why":{"en":"said: 'say' takes no person after it. 'Told' needs a person (told us), and 'said me' is wrong.","tr":"said: 'say' kendinden sonra kişi almaz. 'Told' bir kişi ister (told us); 'said me' yanlıştır.","fa":"said درست است، چون بعد از say شخص نمی‌آید. told شخص می‌خواهد (told us) و said me غلط است."},"hint2":{"en":"Look right after the gap: no person like me or us comes before the reported words. Which reporting verb works without one?","tr":"Boşluğun hemen sağına bak: Aktarılan sözlerden önce me ya da us gibi bir kişi yok. Hangi aktarma fiili kişi olmadan kullanılır?","fa":"بلافاصله بعد از جای خالی را ببین: قبل از حرفِ نقل‌شده شخصی مثل ⁨me⁩ یا ⁨us⁩ نیامده. کدام فعلِ نقل قول بدون شخص به کار می‌رود؟"}},{"from":"hr-2-3","kind":"blank","prompt":"Could you tell me ___ you can work weekends?","options":["do","what","if"],"correct":2,"point":2,"why":{"en":"if: it opens an indirect yes/no question. 'Do' can't sit inside the sentence, and 'what' needs a missing thing.","tr":"if: dolaylı bir evet/hayır sorusu açar. 'Do' cümlenin içinde yer alamaz; 'what' eksik bir şey ister.","fa":"if درست است، چون سؤال بله‌یا‌نهِ غیرمستقیم را باز می‌کند. do داخل جمله جایی ندارد و what دنبال چیزی است که جمله ندارد."}},{"from":"hr-4-2","kind":"mcq","prompt":"Which line in a first-week plan helps a new starter most?","options":["Wednesday: you’ll shadow Hasan on Route 7.","Wednesday: various activities.","Wednesday: you’ll learn a lot."],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"The first: it says what happens and with whom. A new person cannot guess how your company works.","tr":"İlki: Ne olacağını ve kiminle olacağını söylüyor. Yeni biri şirketinin nasıl işlediğini tahmin edemez.","fa":"گزینه‌ی اول: می‌گوید چه اتفاقی می‌افتد و با چه کسی. آدم تازه نمی‌تواند حدس بزند شرکتت چطور کار می‌کند."},"point":1}]}}; })(globalThis.COURSE_FILES = globalThis.COURSE_FILES || {});
